   "text": "Consider the following expression grammar. The semantic rules for expression evaluation are stated next to each grammar production. $\\begin{array}{l} E \\rightarrow \\text {number} \\quad | E$. $\\text {val} = \\text {number}$. $\\text {val} \\\\ \\mid E ^ {\\prime} + ^ {\\prime} E \\mid E ^ {(1)}$. $v a l = E ^ {(2)}$. $v a l + E ^ {(3)}$. $v a l \\\\ \\mid E ^ {\\prime} \\times^ {\\prime} E \\mid E ^ {(1)}$. $v a l = E ^ {(2)}$. $v a l \\times E ^ {(3)}$. $v a l \\\\ \\end{array}$ Assume the conflicts of this question are resolved using yacc tool and an LALR(1) parser is generated for parsing arithmetic expressions as per the given grammar. Consider an expression $\\mathbf { 3 } \\times \\mathbf { 2 } + \\mathbf { 1 }$. What precedence and associativity properties does the generated parser realize?",
   "options": [
    "Equal precedence and left associativity; expression is evaluated to $\\mathrm { ^ 7 }$",
